This extension adds Dishonored: Death of the Outsider modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Automatically installs Void Installer.[/summary]

[size=3][b][color=#ffff00]The extension will automatically download and install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dishonored2/mods/31]Void Installer[/url]. It is a new tool for modding the game and is required for most mods. [/color][/b][/size]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Void Installer installs to the game folder, recognised by a "voidinstaller.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Void Explorer mods with a "voidexplorer.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Void mods with a "modinfo.xml" file and a ".voidindex" or ".voidresources" file install to the "Void Installer\Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Root Game Folder mods with a "base" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Video mods with a ".bk2" file install to the "base\video" folder.[/*]
[*]Save Game mods with a "profile.bin" file or a ".sav" file install to the game's save folder.[/*]
[*]Config mods with a "dishonored_doconfig.cfg" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\Arkane Studios\Dishonored_DO\base" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Includes a tool for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dishonored2/mods/30]Void Explorer[/url]﻿.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff00]Will install mods for Void Installer to "Void Installer&#92;Mods" folder. You need to run Void Installer to complete the installation of these mods. Vortex will give you a notification with a button to run the app after each deployment.[/color][/b][/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Dishonored: Death of the Outsider mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Void Installer:

Recognised when the archive contains a "voidinstaller.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Void Explorer:

Recognised when the archive contains a "voidexplorer.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Void Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modinfo.xml" file and a ".voidindex" or ".voidresources" file.

  Installs to: "Void Installer\Mods"

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── base\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "base" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Video Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".bk2" file.

  Installs to: "base\video"

========================================================================

Save Game Files:

Save files, deployed to the game's save folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "profile.bin".
    - Recognised by any file with the ".sav" extension.

  Installs to: the game's save folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an example save alongside a normal mod makes the archive install as a save.

========================================================================

Config File Mods:

Configuration tweaks, deployed to the game's config location.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "dishonored_doconfig.cfg".

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\Arkane Studios\Dishonored_DO\base"

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping a config file with one of these names inside an unrelated mod makes the whole archive install as a config mod.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
